Microsoft <a href="https://blogs.windows.com/devices/2026/10/07/pre-order-our-most-powerful-surface-devices-ever/">today announced</a> launch timing and pricing for the Surface Laptop Ultra that it unveiled earlier this year.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/surface-laptop-ultra.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1069342" /><br/>
The 15-inch Surface Laptop Ultra is priced starting at &#36;2,599, undercutting Apple's &#36;2,999 16-inch <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macbook-pro/">MacBook Pro</a>, and it targets the same creator and developer market. Microsoft says it is built for "demanding creative, software development, AI, engineering, and 3D workloads."<br/>
<br/>
Microsoft's new laptop uses an Nvidia RTX Spark chip, which includes an Nvidia Blackwell RTX GPU with up to 6,144 cores and an Nvidia Grace CPU with up to 20 cores. It supports up to 128GB of unified memory and has a new thermal architecture to support the hardware. The RTX Spark is an Arm-based chip, so the laptop runs Windows on Arm with x86 apps using Microsoft's Prism emulation.<br/>
<br/>
According to Microsoft, the Surface Laptop Ultra is its most powerful notebook to date. It has the "brightest, sharpest, and most vivid display" Microsoft has used in a Surface device, with peak HDR brightness that's 25% higher than the M5 &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj;'s. The mini-LED display is a touchscreen, and it supports gestures and navigation, but not pen input.<br/>
<br/>
The laptop is lighter than the 16-inch &zwnj;MacBook Pro&zwnj;, with a large haptic trackpad and upgradeable storage. Microsoft even adopted a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/magsafe/">MagSafe</a> equivalent, adding support for Magnetic Connect. Microsoft says Magnetic Connect is the "world's first built-in magnetic USB-C charging on a laptop." The device has three USB-C ports, a USB-A port, an HDMI port, an SD card reader, and a 3.5mm headphone jack.<br/>
<br/>
Along with the Surface Laptop Ultra, Microsoft announced the &#36;5,999 Surface RTX Spark Dev Box to compete with devices like the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/mac-studio/">Mac Studio</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/mac-mini/">Mac mini</a>. It is equipped with an Nvidia RTX Spark chip and offers up to 1 petaflop of AI performance with support for AI models up to 120B parameters.<br/>
<br/>
Microsoft is <a href="https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/surface/devices/surface-laptop-ultra">offering a bonus</a> to customers who "break up" with their MacBooks. MacBook owners can get up to &#36;1,000 cash back when purchasing a Surface Laptop Ultra by trading in an eligible MacBook. The Surface Laptop Ultra launches on October 16.<br/>
<br/>
"We're confident that once today's creators and developers experience everything Surface Laptop Ultra has to offer, they won't look back," reads Microsoft's website.<br/>
<br/>
